---
import Card from "./Card/index.astro";
---

<Card colSpan="md:col-span-1" rowSpan="md:row-span-6" title="About me">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <div class="text-sm font-light">
      <p>
         You may know me from:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
        <li><a class="text-primary-600" href="https://math.columbia.edu/">Columbia University</a>, where I completed my PhD under the supervision of <a class="text-primary-600" href="https://math.columbia.edu/~ccliu">Melissa Liu</a></li>
        <li><a class="text-primary-600" href="https://www.umass.edu/mathematics-statistics/">UMass Amherst</a>, where I completed a senior thesis advised by <a class="text-primary-600" href="https://paulhacking.github.io/">Paul Hacking</a> and also majored in <a class="text-primary-600" href="https://www.cics.umass.edu/">computer science</a></li>
        <li>We may have met at a conference or a seminar.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="text-sm font-light">
      <p class="text-sm font-light">
        My research is in enumerative geometry, especially Gromov-Witten theory. This includes:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
        <li>Higher-genus invariants of Calabi-Yau varieties (using both approaches)</li>
        <li>Higher-genus quantum K-theory (really the K-theory of the moduli of curves)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm font-light">
      Besides doing math, I also enjoy running and playing the piano. I also like to learn about the historical evolution of Chinese dialects.
    </p>
  </div>
</Card>
